    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF, component build, 10-year horizon (routing table row 1: operating software/EDA company; no memory entry -- first valuation). FY0 = FY2026E revenue at the midpoint of the raised guidance ($6.387-6.417B, Q3-2026 call 2026-10-26) because ten of twelve months are reported and the year is guided; year 1 = FY2027. Net debt is the 2026-09-30 balance sheet (Senior Notes carrying 2,483.2 incl. 2027 Notes current 498.8, revolver 150.0, less cash 1,452.0); Q4-2026 cash generation is therefore not credited (small conservatism). Marketable debt (80.7) and equity (10.5) securities are added in equity_bridge. last_fcf = TTM to Q3-2026 owner FCF: reported FCF 1,763.5 (OCF 1,967.9 - PP&E capex 204.4) - SBC incl. withholding 760.3 - interest income 0 = 1,003.2 (16.4% of TTM revenue 6,132). FY2025 owner FCF was 961.9 after the $140.6M DOJ/BIS export-control settlement payment. interest_income set to 0: the company is now net DEBT ($1.18B) after funding the $2.2B cash leg of Hexagon D&E, so there is no cash pile to double count; the flows are built unlevered from EBITDA and net debt is deducted once. Buybacks: a genuine repurchaser ($925M FY2025, $800M 9M-2026, new $2.5B authorization 2026-10-23) -- the flat count is funded, not a convention. Adjusted EBITDA here = GAAP operating income + D&A + SBC + restructuring + settlement loss (FY2023 42.4%, FY2024 42.5%, FY2025 44.0%, 9M-2026 43.9%); it is pre-SBC and SBC is then charged at the combined rate. Working capital: Cadence's OCF has run $110-220M/yr below EBITDA+SBC-cash tax-net interest in FY2023-25 (receivables, unbilled, emulation-hardware inventory), i.e. roughly -20% to -28% of the revenue increase, so wc_capture is NEGATIVE despite deferred revenue. Cash tax: 20% FY2023, 37% FY2024 (Sec.174 capitalisation), 15% FY2025 (OBBBA R&D expensing catch-up), ~34% 9M-2026 on the model EBIT; 26% is the through-cycle rate on an EBIT that already deducts non-deductible withholding taxes. D&A path falls as Hexagon/BETA acquired intangibles (amortisation 9M-2026 $122M) roll off; capex ~3% (FY2025 2.7%, 9M-2026 3.5%). Revenue growth is treated as organic-plus-tuck-in; acquisition spend is not deducted, which is a known generosity for a serial acquirer (see key risks).",
